      "writtenOn": "2018-01-05T17:58:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the purpose of this class is for fetching an object out of a lambda for HIDL, can we use a better / more tailored name than \"Mutable\", eg. HidlResult?\n\nCurrently, the common usages of classes like this\n - duplicate logic, namely checking whether the result code is Result.OK;\n - omit logic out of laziness, eg. enforcing that the result value is null if the result code is anything other than Result.OK\n - don\u0027t keep track of whether or not the result value has ever been set, which is why HidlDeviceManager needs both a MutableInt and a MutableBoolean\n\nPerhaps the value field should be encapsulated (private, accessible only via setters/getters), so that the setters/getters can be responsible for this logic, as well as carry corresponding documentation?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 95,
